apps.changeLog:
## Fixes
- Fix alarm not stopping when dismissed or snoozed (#729):
  - Note: not all devices appeared to be affected by this problem;
- Fix ghost dates in spinner date picker;
- Fix the ripple effect in the alarm editing panel (for the _"Delete alarm once dismissed"_ feature);
- Fix the timer crash if its ringtone is null or inaccessible (#730):
  - The app will now safely play the built-in fallback ringtone instead of crashing;
- Fix some city flags (#725);
- Fix crash for the screensaver (#736);

## Improvements

### General
- Support for live update notifications for timers and the stopwatch (#440):
  - General notes:
    - Available only for Android 16 and above;
    - The display of these notifications must be enabled in the timer and stopwatch settings;
    - If a timer is started at the same time as the stopwatch, the stopwatch time is (unfortunately) the one displayed in the chip. Nothing can be done to fix this;
    - The notification display differs because live update notifications don't allow the use of `RemoteViews`;
    - Regarding grouped notifications: active timers will no longer be grouped together; there will be one group for notifications eligible for display in the chip and another for the rest. Nothing can be done to fix this;

  - Notes for timer notifications:
    - The chip prioritizes displaying the remaining time for the timer closest to expiring;
    - The progress bar updates automatically when 25%, 50% or 75% of the elapsed time is reached;

  - Notes for stopwatch notifications:
    - No progress bar, since there is no end time for a stopwatch;
    - The chip simply displays the stopwatch time, whether it's running or paused;
- Prevent lock screen from hiding active alarm and expired timers;
- Improve animation of timer icon in bottom navigation menu;
- Adjust the ripple effect color for the list items;
- For the black theme in day mode, slightly adjust the background color of the editing panels;
- Improve some layouts and code for a better user experience;

### Alarm
- Add the ability to sort alarms by category (#563):
  - This must be enabled in the settings, where a new category called _"Sorting"_ has been created;
  - Three additional settings have been added: _"Switch to the new category once created"_, _"Display a badge when alarms are enabled"_, and _"Delete alarms when deleting a category"_;
  - The background of the selected category respects the _"Display the card backgrounds"_ and _"Display the background borders"_ settings;
  - Alarms can be assigned to multiple categories;
  - Creating a category with a name that already exists is not permitted, in order to maintain organization;
  - To rename or delete a category, click on it again after selecting it;
- Add the ability to set an alarm to a specific time zone (#217);
- Add the ability to lock alarms (#685);
  - Swipe-to-delete is disabled for these alarms;
  - The alarm features cannot be modified;
  - A padlock icon is displayed on the alarm card to differentiate them from other alarms;
  - These alarms can be displayed at the top of the list (if enabled in the settings) and respect the sorting defined in the _"Sort the alarms"_ and _"Display the enabled alarms first"_ settings;
- Add the ability to snooze alarms every _"x"_ days;
  - Note: 31 days maximum (reasonable value);
- Add the ability to hide info/warning icons in the alarm editing panel;
- Display a tooltip when long-pressing the day of the week buttons;

### Clock
- Add 2 locations for the UTC -9:00 time zone (_Adak_ and _Gambier Islands_);
- Improve city search:
  - Ignore accents when searching for cities;
  - Allow partial matches to find a city by any part of its name;

### Timer
- Add a new button to subtract time from the timer (#327);
- Add the ability to display the timer _"Delete"_ button on the card (#727);

